WEBVTT

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:14.950
<i>Only a few hours remain in this year that was filled with excitement and thrills. {## it's June, man; I'm not feelin it}</i>

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.830
<i>Today is December 31st, New Year's Eve.</i>

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.410
<i>So much has happened this year.</i>

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:27.650
<i>Though I suppose there won't be any more fun as we reach the end. {## preserve contrastive element}</i>

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:31.840
A text.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.200
It's from Pikari.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.930
"Would you like to ring in the new year at Amanchu House?"

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:46.750
There was still fun to be had!

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:52.400
<i>Be sure to eat a light dinner.</i>

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:58.260
<i>This is where everything started for me.</i>

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.790
<i>Tonight will be my first sleepover at Amanchu House.</i>

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.250
<i>There'll be Pikari, and Grandmother, and me.</i>

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.100
<i>It's going to be a wonderful New Year's Eve!</i>

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:15.220
There's so much I wanted to talk to you about

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:15.220
hanashitakatta koto takusan atta no ni

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:20.560
But my mind went blank when I saw your face

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:20.560
kao miru to wasurechau

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:29.170
Every time you peek in to pick me up after school my heart lights up

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:29.170
houkago mukae ni kitekureru no ga ureshikute

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:36.420
I wonder why I so hopelessly feel this way about you

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:36.420
doushite kimi ja nakucha dame na no kana

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:50.170
Maybe it's like how we can't live without the sun or sea

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:50.170
taiyou ya mizu ga hitsuyou na no to niteru ki ga suru

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:50.170
Maybe it's like how we can't live without the sun or sea

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:50.170
taiyou ya mizu ga hitsuyou na no to niteru ki ga suru

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:57.560
The days have begun to get shorter now

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:57.560
hi ga mijikaku nattekita ne

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:05.690
Why must they cut off my time with you?

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:05.690
mou chotto issho ni itai no ni

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:11.300
Tomorrow and the day after, and every day forevermore

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:11.300
ashita mo asatte mo sono saki mo zutto

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:16.450
I want to keep walking home together like this

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:16.450
kouyatte kimi to kaeritai

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:21.900
No matter what the weather was, no matter how my day went

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:21.900
donna tenki demo donna kibun demo

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:29.670
The moment you raise your hand to wave goodbye

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:29.670
mata ne to kimi ga te wo furu toki

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:37.650
I feel like it has been a wonderful day

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:37.650
ii hi datta to omoeru kara

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:44.560
About Thoughts at that
Beginning

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.850
It's so cold!

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.190
Hello...

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:51.640
Oh, we've been waiting for you, Teko!

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:53.520
You must be freezing.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:58.360
Yeah. I came on my scooter, so even with gloves my hands ended up numb.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:02.390
Come in, come in! You can warm right up in front of the heater.

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:03.830
Thanks.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:06.870
Teko-san, welcome.

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:11.240
You're here too, Kodama-chan? It's so nice to see you again. {## 'Long time no see', really}

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:14.430
You too. Hold on, I'll get you some pork soup.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:16.470
Warm up from the inside out! {## if we're gonna give up might as well give up}

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:17.310
Thanks.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:20.930
It's so extravagant.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:24.280
Be sure to save room for the New Year's soba too.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:25.340
Here you are.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:29.270
I'm glad I only had a light dinner like I was told.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:31.730
Teko's a good, well-behaved girl.

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:34.440
So warm!

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:38.610
<i>I get to have such a special New Year's all to myself.</i>

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:45.200
I'm so happy it feels like I'll be hit with misfortune first thing in the new year.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.410
Misfortune?

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:50.230
Was I just thinking out loud?

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.820
I've received your happiness. {## ['because you spoke out loud, i receive your feelings']}

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:56.100
Heya! {## CAMP}

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.090
Hello.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.460
Thanks for coming!

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:01.260
Sup!

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:05.230
Come on in, everyone!

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:06.410
We've been awaiting you!

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:07.990
Thanks for having us!

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:09.430
Pork soup, pork soup!

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:10.520
It smells great!

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:14.180
I must have pork soup to thaw my frozen body! Pork soup, quickly!

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:17.250
Sit tight, I'll dish some right out. {## 'dish' really sounds like a verb to be used with like... not food (PUNISHMENT, primarily), which is ironic, I guess. semantic shift}

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:22.110
My welcome pork soup idea was a huge success! {## -your- welcome pork soup idea?}

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:28.530
There's plenty more where that came from. {## it seriously sounds like she's handing out beatdowns / I'LL DISH SOME RIGHT OUT / PLENTY MORE WHERE THAT CAME FROM}

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:32.460
Isn't it nice having a big, bustling party to ring in the new year, Teko?

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.750
Huh? Oh, yeah, you're right.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:40.600
<i>Yeah, it would be a waste to keep such a fun time all to myself.</i>

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.890
Yay, it's Kokoro-chan!

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:52.490
Good evening.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:55.050
You're here. {## Oh, it's you.}

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:56.520
You came. {## Oh, you.}

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:04.030
Now that everyone's here, I'd like to introduce some of the new faces. {## can you imagine? going to your grandmother's for new year's and being referred to as the newface? my god}

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:07.240
This is my friend, Kokoro-chan.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:09.450
Nice to meet you all.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:13.090
Kokoro-chan, this is my little sister, Kodama-chan.

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:14.300
Nice to meet you.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:20.540
The pajama party she was supposed to have with her friends was cancelled, so she ran over here instead.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:21.420
You don't need to say that much!

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:27.050
My only other option was killing time at home, so I just figured I might as well grace you with my presence.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:29.900
My adorable little sister!

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:30.970
Stop it!

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:32.990
You're all very charming.

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:37.810
Kokoro-chan, you were super cute during Halloween, but you're even cuter today. {## one may as well / 'even' is for contrastive 'but'}

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:39.810
Don't call me cute.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:44.150
Kokoro-chan's goal is to be cool.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:54.700
That's way too cute! {## is this what little kids think is cool}

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:04.240
I have a cat at home too.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:05.890
Oh, no wonder.

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:07.610
You're handling her well.

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:09.600
Kokoro-chan's the coolest!

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:11.350
But adorable when she blushes.

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:13.410
You look happy.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:14.470
I am!

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:18.730
My invitations were all last minute, but everyone still came. {## focus shift}

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.150
I can't contain my smiles!

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:23.350
Me neither!

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:34.170
Otouto-kun is out! {## ZENIN OUTTOOOOOO}

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:34.920
Eh?

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:39.530
Go!

00:06:39.530 --> 00:06:39.930
Fight!

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:41.080
Push, push!

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:42.160
That's it!

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:43.790
It's a draw!

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:48.970
Hold...

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:49.950
Begin! {yeah I'm not making up sumo terms here}

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:53.430
Ring out! {## i'm not going to look this up / surprise hitler}

00:06:56.500 --> 00:07:01.810
<i>It's my last New Year's Eve of middle school, 
but here I am caught up in Onee-chan's plans again.</i>

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:14.490
<i>What a fun and comfortable atmosphere we're all enveloped in. {## or, the orig. minus 'what' / I don't think you can use 'what' like in the original, and if you can, you shouldn't}</i>

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:16.700
Eat up. New Year's soba. {## you know i hate these statements}

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:23.880
<i>Amanchu House has watched over so many smiles.</i>

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:27.590
<i>Over all these years and decades...</i>

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:34.140
<i>Together with Grandmother, in this place. {## this is very strange and I'm not prepared to talk about it right now}</i>

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:42.400
I'm not tired at all, you know...

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:44.020
You should catch some sleep.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:48.190
I can't, I want to do the countdown with everyone...

00:07:57.010 --> 00:07:59.540
Kokoro-chan, I'll take over.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.070
I'm just fine.

00:08:01.070 --> 00:08:04.360
You're bound to get sore sitting in the same position like that.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:06.250
I said I'm fine.

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:12.950
Then how about whoever manages to stay awake longest gets to be Pikari's pillow?

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:14.590
I accept your challenge.

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:20.710
Kodama-chan, are you in middle school?

00:08:20.710 --> 00:08:22.240
Yes, it's my last year.

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:23.750
Then you have exams soon.

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:25.900
Are you applying to Yumegaoka High?

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:30.530
It's my first choice for now. I really like the uniforms. {## ICHIOUUUUUUUUU}

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:33.380
Good, that's a splendid reason.

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:39.240
Then that means our diving club will be welcoming a promising newcomer to our ranks next year!

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:40.860
I'm not sure about that... {## for once I'm on this end, huh}

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:43.750
Really?

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:44.940
Why not?

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:47.670
Don't you like diving?

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:50.550
No, I do, it's just...

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:56.070
The ocean is pretty, and I love to dive,

00:08:56.070 --> 00:09:00.970
but I've always just been following Onee-chan, so basically...

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:04.730
I'm tired of being dragged around by a sister who never thinks before she acts!

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:09.200
On the other hand, I'm jealous of her. {## ENVIOUS ENVIOUSSSSSSSSSSSS}

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:12.490
I always overthink things and can't do anything.

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:16.230
And that's got you hesitant to join the diving club?

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:17.200
Yeah.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:23.160
I don't want to mess up the one chance I get at choosing a club and regret it later.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:27.120
I only get one shot at high school.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:30.960
I know how we can while away the time until New Year's.

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:34.570
Anyone want to hear an old story of mine? {## y/n q so that it can be answered}

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:36.990
Yes, definitely! Please do!

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:40.680
<i>What? Are we just going to forget about me?</i>

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:45.670
I first encountered scuba diving a long time ago.

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:48.900
I was still free diving as an ama back then. {## must avoid, this is like saying 'gyouza dumpling' / I'm serious, aka / other change is to set up for contrastive next sentence, which doesn't work with orig / italics if you want}

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:52.670
But one try, and I was hooked.

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:59.910
It allowed me to go deeper and further into unknown waters that would have been impossible to free dive.

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:03.800
And that's when it came to me.

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:10.530
If I could make scuba diving into a career, I'd be able to get closer to the sea than ever before. {## 'live closer' really sounds like 'physically reside closer', which I don't think is the meaning here}

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:15.010
Heave-ho, heave-ho. {## or just merk it entirely}

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:24.560
Unfortunately, back then most people 
didn't even know what scuba diving was.

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:31.650
Anyone who had anything to do with it at all was a pioneer. That's why... {## the ama weren't pioneers, e.g.}

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:34.570
Good morning!

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:46.330
The local fishermen just couldn't wrap their heads around it. {## but that doesn't mean you regard it as the antichrist, right? no basis for that rudeness}

00:10:47.590 --> 00:10:54.710
Even so, I believed that they'd come to understand someday, 
since they also made their livings from the ocean. {## the fishermen are the referent, and this new structure is to avoid dangling participle}

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:57.670
Okay, time to explore!

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:04.850
The first thing I had to do was learn as much as I could about the sea myself.

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:09.490
And then, after falling even more deeply in love with those waters,

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:16.280
I'd surely discover a sight that would take away the breath of anyone who saw it. {## uh, timing? / TENSE / misplaced away (it'd be at the very end if separated)}

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:23.220
If I found somewhere like that, lots of people would want to come and see.

00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:25.120
That belief kept me going.

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:29.220
However, the sea doesn't give its secrets up so easily. {## there's no mistake to forgive}

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:37.510
Day after day, I dove down into the waters by myself. {## two doubles unnec}

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:42.370
But all I ever found was the same monotonous blue world.

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:46.020
Taken that way, every day was a failure.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:49.580
Kino-chan, you're still doing that?

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:51.190
Everyone's laughing behind your back.

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:53.400
Come and be an ama again.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:56.360
Why? {## this is the same word}

00:11:56.870 --> 00:11:58.700
How could you keep going?

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:01.320
It just goes to show how vast the ocean is.

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:05.360
Time spent complaining was time that could've been put to better use.

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:08.160
Otherwise the sea would never accept me.

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:14.070
Even so, I eventually started to get frustrated.

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:20.010
<i>I'm out of rope. {## what does the rope do}</i>

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:24.830
<i>My tank's half empty too, so I guess this is my limit for the day.</i>

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:28.680
<i>Maybe it's time to give up. {## cool lit, yeah yeah, but there's nothing gained by dodging this}</i>

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:35.270
<i>There's light beyond that ridge.</i>

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:37.080
<i>I want to see.</i>

00:12:38.130 --> 00:12:40.470
<i>No, it's too dangerous...</i>

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:42.560
<i>But...</i>

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:48.530
<i>This is it. This will be the last time.</i>

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:51.450
<i>And only in sight of the rope. {## she left the motherfucker untied? hello? IT'S SWAYING}</i>

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:01.620
You went?!

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:03.450
Isn't that dangerous?

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:05.300
I'm not done yet.

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:12.210
Over the ridge was something like a rift between the rocks. {## chasms go down, they're vertical / 'chasm of rocks' sounds dumb because basically all chasms are, and moreover it's usually a 'chasm in the rocks'}

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:20.700
Wait, don't tell me...

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:22.220
You kept going?

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:26.200
I surfaced and resupplied. {## for reasons, I don't like stock; it's very food}

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:28.660
Thank goodness.

00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:35.250
But the thing is, if I hadn't gone to that place on that day...

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:41.090
If at that time, the sun hadn't been shining down from straight above... {## ugh, whatever, it's in the Japanese}

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:45.760
If at that time, the waters hadn't been calm...

00:13:47.310 --> 00:13:50.460
If I hadn't kept on diving...

00:13:52.570 --> 00:13:56.880
If any one of those hadn't been 
the case, I never would've found it. {## they're not really all 'events' that can 'happen' as it is}

00:13:56.880 --> 00:14:00.250
That miraculous spectacle.

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:08.650
The place I always dove with Onee-chan? {## she doesn't say it, and it's better not to have it said twice}

00:14:08.650 --> 00:14:12.030
That's one of Izu's most famous diving spots! {## can you cut this so that it doesn't overlap PYOOOO?}

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:15.040
Granny, you're the one who discovered it?! {## and it's already here}

00:14:16.590 --> 00:14:18.620
It was one of the happiest days of my life!

00:14:20.060 --> 00:14:21.550
That's amazing!

00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:24.140
It sure was lucky you found it.

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:30.090
Even if I hadn't, that would've been just fine too.

00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:32.100
Huh? But why?

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:36.750
At the time, it felt like every day was a fresh failure,

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:41.610
but I experienced so much just by diving.

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:46.570
It's true that success is often enough by itself. {## is not just contrastive, but contradicts / if it gave value, then there was no value previously}

00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:52.990
But at the same time, you can learn a surprising amount from failure.

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:59.060
It's wasteful to fear failing so much that you can't take action. {## double}

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:03.500
Huh? I didn't realize we were still talking about me...

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:05.500
We never stopped.

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:08.970
Do what you want to do most. {## that kind of inversion feels like the kind of thing I'd pull / changed, though, to allow for more natural exact repetition in the next line}

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:13.470
What I want to do most... {## is play a light music instrument and have tea time after school, trust me}

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:19.490
I want to go diving there too!

00:15:19.490 --> 00:15:20.940
Let's go!

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:23.970
How about going to celebrate when Tekochin gets her Advanced License?

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:25.800
Oh, nice idea!

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:27.170
How's that, Teko?

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:29.410
<i>I guess spending New Year's Eve like this isn't so bad.</i>

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:29.090
Sure, let's do it!

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:51.130
Huh? Ah...

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:54.900
I accidentally fell asleep without realizing it! {## 'at some point' is just... like, obviously it was at -some point- / similar arg apples to 'without realizing it' but less strongly, and this length is a problem}

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:57.580
Oh! You're up, Teko-chan.

00:15:57.580 --> 00:16:00.650
Um... What about the countdown?

00:16:00.650 --> 00:16:04.050
Everyone passed out before midnight. {## i expected better of you, katori}

00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:10.940
Here, amazake. {I'm fine with amazake too}{## it's not the same as sake that's sweet / this is tangential, but on this note: do you ever get the feeling that I'm ironically more conservative than you are? it seems like an inversion of the natural order}

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:13.170
Thank you.

00:16:15.770 --> 00:16:17.320
It's warm.

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:25.170
It's so quiet.

00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:31.650
I've always been bad with big, noisy gatherings like this.

